{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1533416-bloodlines-the-unstatted","id":1533416,"title":"Bloodlines: The Unstatted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-31T06:35:06-07:00","id":1533416,"title":"Bloodlines: The Unstatted","content":"Any bloodlines out there mentioned in the lore but never got a write up at all?<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to homebrew the Ananta Naga and plan to give them Salubri with Assamite sorcerer vibes since they are mentioned as blood sorcerers and assassins. Mentioned they are sort of Salubri since their blood magic creates alchemical concoctions that heal, while they can create deadlier ones as well.<br /> <br /> May name their bloodline gift Amrita.<br /> <br /> Currently thinking of making their set be Auspex, Obfuscate, Resilience, Dominate but I'm not sure if I should keep resilience and just go with celerity to fit with them being assassins.<br /> <br /> Not sure what their bane is like though.<br /> <br /> Since the Kinnari's founder is supposedly Shurpanakha while Lakshamana is Ananta Shesha's avatar, they might be the rivals of the Kinnari thanks to mythology since Lakshamana fought off Shurpanakha in the Ramayana. They probably claim Lakshamana is their founder but like clan/bloodline myths, it's dubious at best.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T11:51:31-07:00","id":1533456,"title":"","content":"Nice thread idea!<br /> <br /> Personally I can only think of the Anubi from &quot;Ancient Mysteries&quot; and &quot;Ancient Bloodlines&quot;. It was an old egyptian Gangrel bloodlines that existed in the time of the Great Covenant among the Bak-ra and Usiri.<br /> <br /> Bak-Ra and Usiri got a full write-up, while the Anubi got a mention and some sentences.<br /> <br /> Till today the Time of the Great Covenant was one of my favorite quasi &quot;Dark Eras&quot;. Never got around to brainstorming more on the setting that was outlined in Ancient Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines for a full Campagne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T13:30:03-07:00","id":1533458,"title":"","content":"I would love to see more bloodlines from the time of the Great Covenant, even unofficial ones. But I haven't really made any myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}